#!/bin/sh
cat <<'TXT'

  dsh-mu is installed. Next steps on this machine:

    1) dsh-muctl doctor          # 31 prerequisite checks (kernel/cgroup/apk/nginx/mirrors)
    2) dsh-muctl install         # packages, DSH runtime, jail template, gateway fragments
       ... which prints a one-time admin password
    3) open http://<this-host>/   and log in, then visit /admin/

  Configuration lives in /etc/dsh-mu/dsh-mu.conf (secrets: secret.key, admin.token).
  Instance data lives in /var/lib/dsh-mu; `apk del` never removes either directory.

TXT
exit 0
